---
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About WorkoutMatch"
  description="Learn why WorkoutMatch focuses on practical workout constraints, what the browser-only product includes, and what it deliberately does not claim."
  path="/about/"
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
  </div>

  <header class="container section-sm about-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this product exists</p>
      <h1>About WorkoutMatch</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        WorkoutMatch starts with the circumstances people actually face: limited
        time, one piece of equipment, a small room, neighbours below, or a
        preference to avoid certain kinds of movement today.
      </p>
    </div>
    <aside class="card card-pad promise">
      <p class="eyebrow">Primary promise</p>
      <p>Choose what you have. Get a balanced workout you can start now.</p>
    </aside>
  </header>

  <article class="narrow about-content">
    <section aria-labelledby="approach-heading">
      <h2 id="approach-heading">A constraint-first approach</h2>
      <p>
        Many workout lists assume a full gym, plenty of floor space, or freedom
        to jump and make noise. WorkoutMatch instead treats equipment, duration,
        space, impact, noise, and position as first-class inputs. A rule-based
        generator then tries to cover complementary movement patterns without
        selecting exercises that violate those choices.
      </p>
      <p>
        The shortest route is the <a href="/quick-workout/"
          >quick workout builder</a
        >. The
        <a href="/generate/">full generator</a> adds goal, experience, detailed environment
        needs, muscle focus, and optional movements to avoid today. Eight <a
          href="/workouts/">curated workout pages</a
        >
        provide substantial static examples when a familiar scenario is enough.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="built-heading">
      <h2 id="built-heading">What is built into the experience</h2>
      <div class="grid-cards">
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <h3>Static information first</h3>
          <p>
            Core explanations, workout examples, exercise instructions,
            formulas, and limitations remain readable as normal HTML.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <h3>Interaction only where useful</h3>
          <p>
            Generation, timers, filters, calculators, and local progress use
            focused browser scripts rather than turning the whole site into a
            client application.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card card-pad">
          <h3>Local by design</h3>
          <p>
            No account or WorkoutMatch cloud sync is required. Personal workout
            and calculator data stay on the device under the boundaries
            explained on the privacy page.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="not-heading">
      <h2 id="not-heading">What WorkoutMatch is not</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It is not a clinician, coach, diagnostic tool, or rehabilitation
          service.
        </li>
        <li>
          It does not promise weight change, calorie burn, fitness outcomes, or
          a perfect workout.
        </li>
        <li>
          It does not create public profiles, rankings, testimonials, or social
          feeds.
        </li>
        <li>
          It does not claim medical or professional review that has not
          occurred.
        </li>
        <li>
          It is not designed for children, teen calculators,
          pregnancy/postpartum programming, or emergencies.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Read <a href="/methodology/">how the rules and equations work</a> and
        <a href="/safety/"
          >how to use general exercise information conservatively</a
        >.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="callout" aria-labelledby="name-heading">
      <h2 id="name-heading">A working name</h2>
      <p>
        WorkoutMatch is a working product name kept in central configuration so
        it can change. The name, associated domain, and brand have not been
        represented as legally cleared.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .promise > p:last-child {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    font-weight: 780;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .about-content > section + section {
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5rem);
  }

  .about-content p,
  .about-content li,
  .about-content article p {
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
  }

  .about-content li + li {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .about-content article p:last-child,
  .about-content .callout p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .about-content .callout h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 50rem) {
    .about-hero {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(18rem, 0.6fr);
    }
  }
</style>
